# Arduino / Waveshare 12.3inch DSI-TOUCH-A - RECOGNISED, NOT SUPPORTED
#
# This file exists so the panel is IDENTIFIED and REFUSED, rather than falling
# through as "no known panel" - which invites forcing another definition onto
# it, and that is the one thing not to do here.
#
# Why it cannot be driven
# -----------------------
# Arduino ships overlays for three panels only:
#
#     display    none, 5-dsi-touch-a, 8-dsi-touch-a, 10-dsi-touch-a
#
# There is no 12.3 inch option and no matching .dtbo on the image. Nor is the
# described-panel path a way round it: that generator emits an overlay for the
# Raspberry Pi style hardware (an ATTINY at 0x45, an edt-ft5x06 touch at 0x38),
# and this panel has a waveshare GPIO chip at 0x45 and a Goodix at 0x5d. It
# would produce a description of hardware that is not present.
#
# The geometry is unlike anything supported. Measured from the touch
# controller's own config block:
#
#     5 inch      720x1280 portrait    cfg 0x46
#     8 inch      800x1280 portrait    cfg 0x82
#     10.1 inch   800x1280 portrait    cfg 0x82
#     12.3 inch   1920x720 LANDSCAPE   cfg 0x5c
#
# Supporting it properly needs DSI timings for the panel from the vendor and a
# new overlay describing Goodix touch plus the waveshare GPIO chip. That is
# real work, not a .panel file, and nothing here can substitute for it.
#
# A warning worth carrying
# ------------------------
# On 2026-09-09 this panel was connected to a board configured for the 5 inch
# overlay - the only configuration available, since none matches it - and it
# smoked. The board was checked afterwards and was undamaged: 0 CCI timeouts,
# no over-current or regulator faults logged, carrier I2C answering normally,
# thermals normal.
#
# The cause was not established. Bad FPC seating and an incompatible power
# pinout are at least as plausible as the overlay, and no fault was logged that
# points either way. What is certain is that driving it with another panel's
# power-up sequence and timings had no chance of working, so there was nothing
# to gain by trying.
#
# Do not select another panel's definition to "see what happens".

PANEL_ID="arduino-12in-touch-a"
PANEL_DESC="Arduino 12.3inch DSI-TOUCH-A (1920x720) - not supported"

# Recognised so it can be refused with a reason. Anything reading this file
# must not install it.
UNSUPPORTED="Arduino ships no overlay for the 12.3 inch panel, and its 1920x720
    landscape geometry matches none of the three that do. Driving it with
    another panel's overlay cannot work. See the notes in this file."

# --- how detect-panel.sh recognises it -------------------------------------
# Same Goodix family as the 8 inch and 10.1 inch, so the product ID identifies
# the family and the touch threshold separates this one: 0x64 here against
# 0x5f (8 inch) and 0x50 (10.1 inch). The release threshold 0x32 is shared with
# the 10.1 inch, which is why the first byte carries the distinction and both
# bytes are read.
DETECT_ADDR="0x5d"
DETECT_WRITE="0x81 0x40"
DETECT_READ="4"
DETECT_EXPECT="0x39 0x32 0x37 0x31"         # ASCII "9271"
DETECT_NOTE="Goodix GT9271, thresholds 64/32, 1920x720 - the unsupported 12.3 inch"

DETECT2_WRITE="0x80 0x53"
DETECT2_READ="2"
DETECT2_EXPECT="0x64 0x32"
